---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>🧑‍🚀 Welcome to my Website!</h1>
			<p> Hello everyone, I am Yan Deng, a current Year 3 Electronics and Electrical Engineering student in 
			University College London. The past 2 years in London has really been an experience of a lifetime. I 
			travelled to so many places, had the craziest experiences, developed some stuff during my time as an 
			engineering student in UCL and had so much more fun. But as I approached the end of my Bachelors, Im 
			starting to feel like Im forgetting some of them. As such, I started this lil project to record some
			of these adventures. (Also I wanted to take this as an opportunity to learn some front end web design,
			such as HTML and CSS) Ill try to include as many projects and experiences as possible as far as I can
			remember, but itll be updating as I move on with my life. 

			</p>

			<h2> About me </h2>
			<p> Abit more about myself, I will like to describe myself as a curious individual. Someone who likes 
			to find out more about the world and how it works functionally. Professionally, my interests include Electronics
			engineering and the aviation industry, with space exploration as one of the goals in my life. In particular, 
			I am interested in development of communication networks utilising space technologies, be in from transmitting information
			down to ground station or between satellites. In my humble opinion, this is what is limiting humans to exchange
			more information, which is essential for us to understand more about Earth during observation, and data transfer
			for scientific research. As such, by working on these, I hope I can contribute to this development. 
			</p> 

			<p>
			Another interest that I have is the development of Unmanned Aerial Systems in the world. This is a rapidly developing
			field, unfortunately exacerbated due to the conflict, and seeing how different implementations of UAS interests me. In 
			particular, I joined my university's UAS team and have since developed aircrafts from scratch, namely quadcopter, VTOL Fixed wing
			and a Blended Wing Body. I have an interest in the electronics side of it, in particular choosing electronic components
			and programming and tuning parameters on the Flight Controller with Mission Planner to achieve the intended goal. 
			In the meantime, it also gave me a glimpse to the mechanical side of aircraft development, such as the techniques
			involved in validating an aircraft design, and the aerodynamic considerations when developing one. 
			</p>

			<p> On a less professional note, I really enjoy watching football. To me, football is about rhythm and control, in which
			there can be stretches with not much action, but the minor details can reveal a lot on the teams strategy and performance. 
			I also enjoy creating music and playing instruments, figuring out chord progressions and understanding how music works 
			from a technical perspective. Lastly, my childhood interest, Pokemon, Ive gotten into competitive battling during my JC days
			and I still participate in online tournmanets on Showdown, althought not as often now. 

			</p>
			
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
